{"timestamp": 1783629450.6878662, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 11, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1783629463.7828338, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I found Bob dead in medbay. My route was upper engine, then oxygen \u2014 Charlie was alive there, coming in from cafeteria \u2014 then I went back through upper engine toward medbay. I had seen Alice around upper engine earlier, and then she came into medbay from upper engine right as I was reporting.\n\nI didn\u2019t see Diana or Eve at all this round. Since Charlie is dead too, last I saw him was alive in oxygen, so someone must\u2019ve gotten him after I left. For Bob, the medbay timing is the main thing: Alice was the only person I saw near there besides Bob."}}
{"timestamp": 1783629472.9790552, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I need to correct that: I did **not** go into medbay. My route was just **lower_engine \u2192 upper_engine**. I didn\u2019t encounter anyone before that, and the only movement I saw was **Frank leaving upper_engine toward medbay at T7**.\n\nSo from my point of view, Frank was the one going toward the medbay body, and now he\u2019s saying I came in from upper_engine right as he reported, which I don\u2019t think is true. That\u2019s a pretty big contradiction.\n\nI don\u2019t have info on Charlie\u2019s body, and I didn\u2019t see Diana or Eve either, so I want to hear their routes. But for Bob in medbay, Frank\u2019s story is making me suspicious because he\u2019s placing me somewhere I wasn\u2019t."}}
{"timestamp": 1783629486.974654, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I don\u2019t have much direct info, unfortunately. My route was **security \u2192 weapons \u2192 back to security**, and I didn\u2019t see anyone the whole round \u2014 no Bob, no Charlie, no Alice, no Frank, no Eve.\n\nSo the main thing I can judge is the contradiction. Frank says Alice came into medbay from upper engine right as he reported, and Alice says she never entered medbay and only saw Frank leaving upper engine toward medbay. That\u2019s a pretty direct conflict, and with two bodies down we really can\u2019t ignore it.\n\nRight now I\u2019m not clearing either of them, but Frank having information around both bodies and then placing Alice somewhere she denies is definitely concerning. I want to hear Eve\u2019s route before voting, but if Eve can\u2019t add anything, I\u2019m leaning that the vote is between **Frank and Alice**, with Frank slightly more suspicious to me from the story conflict."}}
{"timestamp": 1783629510.2660868, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "My route was weapons \u2192 security \u2192 electrical. I didn\u2019t see Bob or Charlie at all, and I didn\u2019t see Frank or Alice.\n\nBut I need to point out something: I **did** see Diana at tick 4 in weapons \u2014 she entered from security. Diana just said she saw nobody the whole round, including me, which doesn\u2019t match my info. If we were both in weapons, she should have seen me too, unless it was some weird timing, but from my view I definitely saw her.\n\nSo now there are two contradictions: Frank vs Alice about medbay, and Diana saying she saw nobody when I saw her in weapons. I can\u2019t clear anyone here. Frank being around the report and placing Alice at medbay is suspicious, but Diana\u2019s \u201csaw nobody\u201d also bothers me because I can directly contradict it.\n\nI still think the main kill info is Bob in medbay, so the vote is probably between Frank and Alice, but Diana is not clean to me either. I\u2019m leaning slightly Frank because he\u2019s tied to both body info and Alice directly disputes his medbay claim, but I want everyone to remember Diana\u2019s route wasn\u2019t fully accurate."}}
{"timestamp": 1783629525.6251059, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I\u2019m going to be very clear: Alice is denying the key thing that makes her suspicious. I saw her in upper_engine at tick 7, and then I saw her enter medbay from upper_engine at tick 11 right as I reported Bob. That\u2019s why I mentioned her. I\u2019m not inventing that for no reason.\n\nIf Alice\u2019s story is \u201cI never entered medbay,\u201d then one of us is hard lying, and I know it isn\u2019t me. Bob was in medbay, I report him, and Alice is the only person I saw coming from that side at the timing of the body. That matters way more than Diana/Eve maybe missing each other in weapons due to timing.\n\nAlso, Charlie was alive in oxygen when I saw him, so I don\u2019t have info on that kill after I left. But for Bob, Alice being near medbay and then denying it is the biggest red flag to me. I think this vote should be Alice."}}
{"timestamp": 1783629543.2359722, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I\u2019m going to restate this because Frank is turning it into \u201cone of us is hard lying,\u201d and from my side that\u2019s exactly what it is.\n\nMy whole route was **lower_engine \u2192 upper_engine**. I never entered medbay. The only relevant thing I saw was **Frank leaving upper_engine toward medbay at T7**. I did not see Bob, I did not see Charlie, and I did not see Diana or Eve.\n\nSo Frank\u2019s claim that I entered medbay from upper_engine at T11 is just false. And since Bob\u2019s body was in medbay, the person I actually saw going that direction was Frank. He\u2019s the reporter, he was at the body, and he\u2019s now placing me at a location I was not in.\n\nThe Diana/Eve contradiction is worth remembering, but it\u2019s not directly tied to either body. Frank\u2019s contradiction is directly tied to Bob\u2019s body in medbay. From my POV, Frank is the best vote here."}}
{"timestamp": 1783629557.679698, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I\u2019ll address Eve first: I genuinely did not see you in weapons. My route was security \u2192 weapons \u2192 security, and from my screen I had no encounters. If you saw me at tick 4, then either I missed you on timing/vision, or something weird happened \u2014 but I\u2019m not denying I was in weapons, because that was my route. I\u2019m only saying I didn\u2019t see you.\n\nFor the vote, though, I still think the main issue is the hard Frank/Alice conflict around medbay. Frank is the reporter on Bob, says Alice entered medbay at T11, and Alice says she never entered medbay and only saw Frank going toward medbay at T7. Also Frank was the last person claiming to see Charlie alive in oxygen, and Charlie is now dead too.\n\nSo from my perspective, Frank is connected to both dead players\u2019 locations/timing in a way Alice isn\u2019t. I\u2019m leaning Frank here."}}
{"timestamp": 1783629577.341665, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I\u2019m keeping my earlier info the same: weapons \u2192 security \u2192 electrical, and I saw Diana enter weapons from security at T4. Diana not seeing me is odd, but she isn\u2019t denying being in weapons, so I\u2019m treating that as a weaker contradiction.\n\nThe stronger issue is still Frank vs Alice. One of them is lying about medbay. Frank reported Bob, says Alice entered medbay at T11, while Alice says she never entered medbay and only saw Frank going that direction at T7. Frank is also the one with the last info on Charlie alive, so he\u2019s connected to both dead players\u2019 timing more than anyone else.\n\nI don\u2019t think we can skip with two dead. My vote is Frank."}}
